# Which browsers autoprefixer targets, and what `npm run build` compiles for.
#
# The floor is set by iOS Safari, not by the desktop browsers: this is a
# dashboard people open on a phone, and iOS Safari is both the most common
# mobile engine and the slowest to gain features. 15.4 (March 2022) is the
# release that added the dynamic viewport units the layout relies on, so
# anything older would fall back to the 100vh behaviour those units exist to
# avoid.
#
# Run `npx browserslist` to see exactly which versions this resolves to.

defaults
iOS >= 15.4
Safari >= 15.4
not dead
